IMPLEMENTATION ERROR, recorded rather than discarded. ols_exact() coerced each float to a Fraction via limit_denominator(10**12). Summing 13391 such fractions makes the running denominator the lcm of thousands of unrelated 12-digit integers, so the "exact" least squares never terminated inside its budget. The run produced NO deliverable and NO measurement, and NOTHING from it is reported anywhere.
It is an implementation_error and not a resource_exhaustion: the machine was adequate and the algorithm was wrong.
SUPERSEDED BY RUN-ECQSTR-827765-010, which drops limit_denominator and uses the EXACT binary Fraction of each float, whose denominators are powers of two and whose lcm is therefore just the largest of them.
The producer sent SIGTERM at 470 s and the process was reaped; this record was written by hand from the observed state rather than by the run harness, and that is disclosed here.
